Let G=(S,T,S\times T) be a complete bipartite graph with |S|=|T|=n. Associate \alpha_i\in\mathbb R with each i\in S and \beta_j\in\mathbb R with each j\in T. Given integrable functions f and g, define
w_{ij}=\begin{cases}\displaystyle\int_{\alpha_i}^{\beta_j}f(y)\,dy,&\alpha_i\leq\beta_j,\\[4pt]\displaystyle\int_{\beta_j}^{\alpha_i}g(y)\,dy,&\beta_j<\alpha_i.\end{cases}
A matching problem with these edge weights is called a Gilmore\text{–}Gomory matching problem.

